ly play a strong combination and gain momentum with their 9-card advantage.\n\nReason:\nI should **play ♣2** to take control. While it uses my strongest card, it\'s crucial to prevent the landlord from getting free play with a 9-card hand. After playing ♣2, I\'ll have initiative to lead, and I can play ♠10, ♦Q, or ♥A as singles, forcing responses. This maintains pressure on the landlord rather than letting them dictate the game flow.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣2"]}'}
