nning potential\n\nReason:\nI should play ♦Q rather than ♥A. By playing my weaker card first, I maintain flexibility. If the landlord beats ♦Q, my teammate gets a chance to contribute, and I still hold the powerful ♥A. If the landlord passes (has 3 cards but can\'t/won\'t beat Q), I can finish with ♥A on the next turn. This strategy balances aggression with risk management and keeps my strongest card as insurance.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦Q"]}'}
